      "writtenOn": "2025-05-27T18:03:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we still expect + anticipate that it\u0027s more efficient than what we currently do?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1127,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 1127,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "edf940d8f7007445b4bebc47d7ed08b7a2f03a76",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c4e1492_7ad3a2a3",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1127,
      "author": {
        "id": 20444
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-27T20:40:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not very familiar with the inner workings of Graphite yet, so I can\u0027t be certain, but I suspect yes the front-end can do better. Like render steps can probably have a small packed description of what state they need (since I imagine lots of the state is tied together) then diffing the state is faster than the backend doing equality checks on every bit of state.",
      "parentUuid": "d713796e_2846b0b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1127,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 1127,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "edf940d8f7007445b4bebc47d7ed08b7a2f03a76",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9b549b6_f2f2ac59",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1127,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T15:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we can definitely do something more efficient here, possible similar to the RenderStep ID check in the next change for dynamic vertex attributes.\n\nI don\u0027t think checking render step ID is ideal here, though, because there are far fewer sets of DepthStencilSettings values that are used by all of the RenderSteps.  The ones chosen are defined in CommonDepthStencilSettings.h so we could easily assign them IDs or stable addresses to make a quick equality check trivial.",
      "parentUuid": "1c4e1492_7ad3a2a3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1127,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 1127,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "edf940d8f7007445b4bebc47d7ed08b7a2f03a76",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50763d17_948aa05f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1127,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T17:18:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree the front end is likely to do better than the backend performing these checks - I moreso wonder about whether using the dynamic state in this way as opposed to not at all (as we do now). I was just curious if you had confidence that this would be an improvement even if we are delegating this work in a less efficient way to just the Vulkan backend for now, though I think that\u0027s answered via Michael\u0027s comment.",
      "parentUuid": "1c4e1492_7ad3a2a3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1127,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 1127,
        "endChar": 98
